Ruby-ShapeLib licensing
======================

Code and documentation
----------------------

Ruby-ShapeLib is available under either the MIT license (LICENSE-MIT) or
the GNU Library General Public License version 2.0 (LICENSE-LGPL), at
your option. SPDX expression: MIT OR LGPL-2.0-only.

Originally authored by prasinos@users.sourceforge.net, with contributions
from Mike Mangino, Mike Perham, Nick Estes, and other contributors.

The original README offered LGPL or Shapelib's MIT-style default license.
The original author's project identifies LGPL version 2.0 and MIT:
https://sourceforge.net/projects/ruby-shapelib/

The native Shapelib C library is installed separately and retains its own
license notices: https://github.com/OSGeo/shapelib

Bundled test data
-----------------

The files in test/data/ZillowNeighborhoods-CA/ are Neighborhood Boundaries
in California, published October 1, 2007. Zillow.com compiled this data
with the help of municipalities throughout the United States.
Source: http://www.zillow.com/

This dataset is redistributed without modification under Creative Commons
Attribution-ShareAlike 3.0 Unported (CC-BY-SA-3.0). Its original attribution
and license information are retained in ZillowNeighborhoods-CA.shp.xml.
See LICENSE-CC-BY-SA-3.0 and https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/.

The dataset's license is separate from the code's alternative licenses.
The gemspec lists all three identifiers because the package includes both
the code and the dataset.
